course: dictionary
lesson: 15919
title: Unpigmented: without natural colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pigment is the natural colouring in things such as skin, hair, eyes, leaves and paint. Unpigmented means without that pigment, so it looks white, pale or clear. The un- at the front means "not", so unpigmented means "not pigmented".
explain: «The albino mouse had unpigmented white fur and pink eyes.» The clue is white. The fur has no pigment, so it has no normal colour. Try the swap: "The albino mouse had without-colour white fur" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: «The unpigmented patches on the leaf looked pale yellow.» The leaf has coloured parts and pale parts. The pale parts are the ones without pigment. Look for the word that sounds like "not" in the front of the word, and you have half the meaning already.
fact: Pigment is the natural colouring found in skin, hair, eyes, plants and paint.
fact: «Unpigmented» means without pigment, so it looks white, pale or clear.
fact: The prefix un- means "not", so unpigmented means "not pigmented".
fact: Melanin is a pigment that colours skin and hair.
fact: Chlorophyll is a pigment that colours leaves green, and parts of a leaf without it look pale.
exercise: «The albino mouse had unpigmented fur.» What does unpigmented mean here? | Wet and muddy | Very long | *Without natural colour, so the fur looks white | Dyed bright blue
exercise: Which pigment colours leaves green? | Sunlight | *Chlorophyll | Rain | Melanin
exercise: In art, what does an unpigmented paint base look like? | Loud and bumpy | Red and gold | Black | *Clear
test: «The unpigmented patches on the leaf looked pale.» Why do these patches look pale? | Because they were painted white by hand | Because they are very old | Because they have no pigment | *Because they have no pigment, and no pigment means no colour
test: In the word unpigmented, what does the un- mean? | *Not | Again | Before | Full of
exam: «Albino animals have unpigmented fur and pink eyes.» Why does the fur look white? | Because it is wet | Because it is painted | *Because it has no natural colouring | Because it is very old
